														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3791703">
									

<p>Author, a concern has been raised regarding this article, specifically that it seems to possess a couple similarities to a work that was posted in 2017, <a href="/scp-3994">SCP-3994</a>.</p>
<p>Of note:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Aside from concept (formation of shells/skin), there are some containment procedure similarities (ex. &quot;15 per chamber&quot; vs &quot;12 per chamber&quot;) and other description similarities (having an amorphous and gelatinous/viscous mass disguised as a human, poor grammar/hold of human language, inability to pass as a human being, formation and decay of a shell, interview between an instance and a researcher).</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This seems to be due to coincidence, so I'm not particularly inclined to order you to change it; however, since the concern was raised I believe it would be good to hear an explanation from you.</p>

							</div>

								
					
